  "title": "PRIOS",
  "description": "The PRIOS dataset contains electrocorticography (ECoG) recordings from 6 patients aged 13-53 years. Cortico-cortical evoked potentials (CCEPs) were elicited by single pulse electrical stimulation (SPES), both in the awake patient during clinical routine and under general propofol anesthesia in the operating room. The data support investigation of how propofol affects local effective brain networks.",
  "methods_description": "CCEPs were recorded with subdural ECoG during single pulse electrical stimulation, either in the awake state for clinical purposes (SPES-clinical) or under propofol anesthesia (SPES-propofol). Electrode positions were estimated by running Freesurfer on each subject's MRI and converted to MNI305 space using the Freesurfer surface-based non-linear transformation.",
